    "notes": [
      [
        18,
        175,
        "INPUT CONTRACT\nSolar: Voltaic P105, 6V class, expected ~5W / Vmp6.01V / Voc7.07V; raw panel, no USB regulator.\nDC: regulated or fused 9-16V battery source; NOT an automotive load-dump qualified input.\nD101/D102 provide source ORing, reverse-polarity blocking and prevent DC feeding the panel.\nHigher-voltage DC normally wins. Both inputs may be connected. Grounds are common.\nSMBJ16A: 16V standoff, specified clamp26V at rated pulse; replace old SMBJ26A.\nTVS is AFTER blocking diodes; reversed input must not forward-bias the TVS.\nF101/F102 protect wiring; coordinate source fault current/fuse/TVS energy during bench validation.\nBoard connectors are internal JST PH pigtail landings; external weatherproof connector remains mechanical scope.\nNo input bypasses the cell: system operation requires a valid battery."
      ]
